## Defining data: `{{DATA:key}}value{{/DATA}}`

Like WordPress custom fields, you can define data under a named key.

```
{{DATA:key}}value{{/DATA}} : defines data (shown)
{{DATA:key:GHOST}}value{{/DATA}} : defines data (hidden via GHOST)
```

```
Example:
### {{DATA:BOOK_TITLE}}Programming PHP{{/DATA}}
Author: {{DATA:AUTHOR}}Taro Yamada{{/DATA}}
{{DATA:ISBN:GHOST}}978-1234567890{{/DATA}}
```
Define data using this format. Here's how it's rendered on the page:
Since ISBN is set to GHOST, it isn't displayed.
It works like a form's `type="hidden"` attribute.

### {{DATA:BOOK_TITLE}}Programming PHP{{/DATA}}
Author: {{DATA:AUTHOR}}Taro Yamada{{/DATA}}
Price: ¥{{DATA:PRICE}}2800{{/DATA}}
{{DATA:ISBN:GHOST}}978-1234567890{{/DATA}}

